<title>POLAND: Most Polish min T-bill prices rise, 52-week flat.</title>
<headline>Most Polish min T-bill prices rise, 52-week flat.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills rose at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.714 billion zlotys against a 1.1 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 1.09 billion of its bills on Monday.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---     94.75    90.03     ---     81.85</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (94.76)  (90.02)    ---    (81.85)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---     95.28    90.10     ---     82.07</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.30)  (90.20)    ---    (82.20)</p>
<p>   offer		---     300.0    200.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---     427.9    382.4     ---     903.9</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---     300.0    200.9     ---     589.1</p>
<p>   next auction*    ---	---     100.0     ---     300.0</p>
<p>@ NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.(*) The ministry announced it would hold an extra tender on Wednesday, April 16. The payment date for that tender is Friday, April 18.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
